French TV exec says Vivendi tapped him for CFO

A French television executive said on Tuesday he had been approached about taking over as finance chief at beleaguered media giant Vivendi Universal -- and acknowledged the job would be a ""challenge.""

Jacques Espinasse, chief operating officer at French satellite TV consortium TPS, has been cited by the French press as a candidate for the financial hot seat at Vivendi, which is grappling with cash and debt problems in the wake of the sacking earlier this month of chairman Jean-Marie Messier.
