2565,"Re: Dragging image from Google Chrome crashes onto Java application crashes it (Trial Version)","
On 5. apr. 2010, at 19.34, Doug Zwick wrote:

> I put an additional try/catch around the code interpreting the x-java-image flavour. If that attempt fails, I fall back to one of the file path or URL string flavours. It's ugly, and only really practical because the code has to be able to handle drag sources that only put an URL or file path in the Transferable. 

That does of course work, but you might run into issues with protected resources, as you won't be able to share credentials/sessions/etc with the browser (unless you get a path to the browsers locally cached version of the resource). 

I did some extra testing on this topic, and found there are more things going wrong: The ""image/x-pict"" flavor, which should contain a TIFF encoded version of the image, instead contains only a null-terminated string ""Unsupported type"". It's probably caused by the same underlying problem that leads to the Error in the ""image/x-java-image"" case though, but might help locating the bug. 


Best regards,

-- 
Harald K

