3342,"Re: Kde 3.5 ... (Trial Version)","Am Dienstag 11 Mai 2010 schrieb Mike Bird:
> On Mon May 10 2010 15:20:52 Martin Steigerwald wrote:
> > This list is not for development issues like developing / maintaining
> > KDE 3.5 packages for Squeeze.
> > 
> > So IMHO any further request for KDE 3.5 in Squeeze is off topic on
> > this list as Debian KDE/Qt maintainers repeatedly said they won't.
> 
> Please don't lie.  This list is for ""Discussions related to KDE in
> Debian. Those developing KDE-based packages are encouraged to use this
> to discuss issues and share their experience.""
> http://lists.debian.org/debian-kde/

First its IMHO.

Second its from what I understood about the different purposes of debian-
kde and qt-kde-ml mailing lists.

And debian-kde is clearly sorted as users mailing list:

Debian in KDE
http://lists.debian.org/users.html

debian-qt-kde: Packages using Qt and/or KDE
http://lists.debian.org/devel.html

So I think my view is not that far off.

So or so: Your posts did not seem to me to bring anyone even the slightest 
bit forward towards having KDE 3.5.

So I finish with a suggestion, how this can work:

---------------------------------------------------------------------
Hi developers and users of Debian in KDE,

I set up an Alioth project repository of KDE 3.5 packages that I forward-
ported to Squeeze at:

http://some-alioth-url

Right now I started just with the forward port of the basic KDE packages.

I like to continue that work and to make the package co-installable with 
KDE 4. 

I appreciate any helping hand. If you are a user and want to use KDE 3 I 
encourage you to try may package. Please note they are not co-installable 
with KDE 4 in the moment. If you are a developer please help me with 
building and polishing packages.

If you want to help out, subscribe to mailinglist xyz.

Regards,
Mike
---------------------------------------------------------------------

Now, how about that, Mike? How about being the change you want to achieve?

Thanks.

Note: KDE 3.5 doesn't really need to be co-installable for those only 
interested in KDE 3.5. At least not initially.

Just a small start might pull this off for you. But if you do not *act*, 
probably nothing will happen. You can't change those who are not 
interested in providing KDE 3.5 for Debian Squeeze. So either you start 
pulling it off for yourself or it - unless someone else feels the 
motivation to do it - *will just not happen*.

Its as easy as that.

Ciao,
-- 
